Dear Douglas,

We have completed the review of LNDE-RPT-96-014 regarding the 118 CMLs measured while the unit was not yet in service. With the first amine circulation now underway at the ATU-100, I have formally accepted this baseline thickness survey for our asset integrity records.

As these readings represent the initial state, they will serve as the basis for calculating future corrosion rates and remaining life per site rules. Based on the Class 2 service designation for amine, the next thickness measurement will be scheduled within the 10 year maximum interval.

